              <p> 
              </p><p> <font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><b>PMWATCH</b> 
                -- May 7, 2002 -- 
As the text below shows clearly (inside text box), Israel has grossly violated
the most basic tenets of the Geneva Conventions in its latest assault on Palestinians.  
In other words, Israel has perpetrated war crimes.
</font></p><p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">
And yet, not one editorial so far in the US media has even bothered to mention that Israel
has violated these very important conventions.  Instead, if and when Israel is
criticized, the criticism is over tactical matters: i.e., that Ariel Sharon is 
not helping things by brutalizing the populations (true enough), but never that
Ariel Sharon should cease and desist because his actions are war crimes.
              </font></p><p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> Please press 
                the media to do the moral thing: to stand up and decry war crimes -- 
as they have done against China in Tibet, against Milosevic in Bosnia, against Saddam
(when he became an enemy, that is) in Iraq, etc,. </font> 
              </font></p><p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">Your letter 
                will be sent to:</font> 
